    init-agents now validates the managed-marker structure of AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md before writing anything. Malformed markers — zero-or-many pairs, reversed order, an unterminated block — are rejected with an actionable error and no writes at all, instead of a raw byte-offset replacement that could clobber user-owned text. Non-regular files in place of an instruction file are rejected the same way, naming what was found (`found directory`, not the permission-bit form).

    Pointer updating is refactored into pure rendering, so every byte written is computed from the validated snapshot read before any file is touched. Claude import detection sees that same snapshot.

    Alias behavior is preserved throughout: symlinks, hard links and dangling symlinks in either direction are written exactly once.

